today we're going to be speaking with  Jeffrey Mandel who's President and Lead  counsel at law forward the firm that  filed the landmark lawsuit against the  fraudulent 2020 electors in Wisconsin uh  really great having you on I appreciate  your time  thanks so much David it's great to be  here so just to get everybody kind of up  to speed we saw attempts at this fake  elector scam in a number of different  states Arizona is one place where it  made a lot of news the concept was even  though Joe Biden won what if we we  meaning typically some Republicans what  if we just send Republican electors to  say we're giving our electoral votes to  Donald Trump anyway that's the gist of  it is that right  that is the gist of it it requires us  stepping back and sort of thinking back  to Schoolhouse Rock and our basic  understanding of students we all think  that every fourth November we go to the  polls and we vote for a candidate for  president right people say did you vote  for Biden or did you vote for Trump but  in reality you're voting for a slate of  electors who will represent your state  in the Electoral College it is not the  popular vote it is that Electoral  College vote that chooses the president  and so what we had was seven states  where even though the popular vote said  that the electors pledged to Joe Biden  and Kamala Harris would represent that  state in the Electoral College  nonetheless electors who were pledged to  Donald Trump and Mike Pence chose to  meet and submit papers claiming that  they were actually the valid qualified  and duly elected electors for their  state so in Wisconsin for example what  that meant was we had 10 individuals and  as you know they're mostly Republican  party bigwigs who decided that they knew  better than 3.3 million of their  neighbors a record 3.3 million  wisconsinites voted in 2020 and these 10  people decided that they didn't care  what those other 3.3 million people  thought they were going to take it upon  themselves to hijack Wisconsin's  participation in choosing the next  president  now when we talk about the January 6th  committee there's an investigation  happening in Georgia Etc the question of  criminality of some of the different  things that were attempted is is often  brought up to be clear you have filed a  lawsuit that seeks damages the  criminality question is a different one  when it comes to these schemes is that  right  that's right and I do think that uh at  least here under Wisconsin state law and  around the country under federal law I  think that there is a likelihood that  many of these people committed crimes  and could be prosecuted and potentially  uh put in jail but what we're filing is  a civil lawsuit that seeks civil  remedies  um and will be a way of trying to learn  more about exactly what did happen here  in Wisconsin and how it worked because a  civil lawsuit comes with Discovery the  opportunity to see documents to take  depositions and have testimony I'm  trying to think back you know there was  this kind of circus tour that went  around the country that involved Rudy  Giuliani and Jenna Ellis and sometimes  Sydney Powell and others did did that  circus go through Wisconsin around the  same time that the fake elector scam was  being kind of conceived  well the circus never came fully to town  here in Wisconsin  um you know Rudy Giuliani for example to  my knowledge never came uh to Wisconsin  we did have one of Sydney Powell's uh  Kraken lawsuits yes mainstream  conspiracy theories here in Wisconsin  and what's interesting about that I mean  there are lots of things that are  interesting about that but one of the  things that's interesting about that is  the plaintiff that Sydney Powell  represented in that lawsuit is one of  the fraudulent electors right  um here in Wisconsin so all of this is  tied together and so the circus came to  town through the courts but it never  came to town with the with the full  media Entourage so in terms of your  lawsuit I mean what are you alleging  what are the damages who who was uh  damaged so to speak  sure so we represent um three plaintiffs  two of them were actually the among the  valid electors for Joe Biden and Kamala  Harris okay one of them is a voter who  feels strongly that these people tried  to disenfranchise her and steal the  value of her vote by going against the  will of the voters and what we're doing  is we're using some old established  common law ideas to try to get at this  conduct fundamentally the problem is  nobody ever thought that someone would  try something as audacious as what these  fake electors did in these seven states  so there is no law that says you can't  do that because we don't pass laws that  tell people not to do things that nobody  would ever imagine someone would do and  that has led to this challenge of saying  no matter who we talk to when we explain  what the fraudulent electors did  everyone says oh that can't be right  that can't be legal  um that offends my most basic sense of  fair play and Civic understanding of  democracy right but there isn't a  specific law so what we've done is we've  taken some very old principles from the  common law and said that we think that  these fit so one of them is public  nuisance right our election system and  our democracy is a finely calibrated and  and somewhat fragile structure that is  for the public good and there is a  long-standing idea that if if if I take  private action that harms the public  good  um someone can try to stop me using an  adoption that says that I'm creating a  nuisance to the public for my own  benefit but everyone else is detriment  so we're using that theory uh we're  using a theory of civil conspiracy that  these is 10 electors and thus far we've  also named two lawyers who assisted them  and we might need to add more people as  as we find out who else was involved  right the January 6 committee recently  made quite clear that Senator Johnson  seems to be involved  um but that these people conspired  to break the law whether they ultimately  did break the law right that's sort of  the criminal question but the fact that  they were trying to break the law that  they were trying to convince Congress  to take these papers that in itself we  think is actionable and there is a long  long standing idea  um and I apologize for the Latin but it  goes under the name of  this is a red an order that you could go  to for hundreds of years to courts if  you were supposed to serve in a public  office but someone else was occupying  that office and keeping you out of it  and so we are bringing a a a claim for  such an order on behalf of the actual  electors that these other people have  tried to usurp that office and by saying  we Trump fraudulent electors we're the  real electors they are implicitly saying  that the Biden electors are liars and  are are not the real electors and so  we're also bringing a claim under under  that here have the um have the have the  fraudulent electors had to personally  lawyer up as a result of this at this  point  they have so um they've all hired  Council and we're in those early stages  of lawsuits as you know David you know  litigation can be kind of slow yes so  we're in the early stages of the the  lawyer sort of maneuvering we filed in  State Court they would rather be federal  court which is not where this case  belongs and so we're in the process of  bringing it back to State Court what  kind of uh damages and restitution are  you seeking here  so we're seeking a number of things um  first we're seeking a clear and uh  unambiguous order from a court that what  happened here was improper and unlawful  and it should never happen again  second we are seeking an order that  would prohibit any of these people from  ever being involved with the Electoral  College in Wisconsin again because it  seems to me that they have abused the  privilege of being part of our Civic  Fabric and they should they should not  have that opportunity again I agree um  third  we are seeking  um deterrence we want accountability and  we want deterrence we never want to see  this happen again and so we are seeking  punitive damages for the fact that these  folks um deliberately interfered in the  legal rights of the real electors and  under Wisconsin law those punitive  damages could be up to 200 000 for each  of the defendants have you been in touch  with potential uh with lawyers that are  potentially looking at doing this in  other states where these schemes were  hatched  we've certainly uh We've certainly had  some conversations and some Outreach it  is my hope I really believe that both  accountability and deterrence are  essential so this doesn't happen again  and so it is my hope that we will see uh  cases like this in all of the states one  of the big questions is if whoever had  followed through on this like if these  electors had gotten on a plane or you  know what whatever the the real attempt  was a bona fide attempt what would have  happened like could could they have said  no we we believe that Trump gets these  votes and then what would have happened  I mean John Eastman wrote this memo of  how what Pence could do he's now in  legal Jeopardy himself he's had to  lawyer up the FBI recently sees this  phone you know he's got his fair share  of problems for even suggesting this  framework but there's this question of  like if they both show up then then what  would have happened  well I mean the reality is we came a lot  closer to that than than we'd like to  think because I think your intuition  that the Electoral College happens in  Washington is a common one but that's  actually not right  the Electoral College happens in each  state's capital at the same time on the  same date and so when these fraudulent  electors met in Madison on December 14th  of 2020 and they and they signed these  papers claiming to be the real electors  and when that happened in Arizona and in  Georgia and in Michigan and in Nevada  and in Pennsylvania and in New Mexico  that that was the thing they submitted  these papers that's the act in other  words like the real electors did it on  that day and the fake electors did and  then so at that point it's it's it but  they've both done it  that's absolutely right and it really  all came down to to then vice president  Pence  um if he had followed John Eastman's uh  wishes and been willing to credit those  votes then we would have seen um chaos  we would have seen how Congress reacted  uh we've seen uh almost certainly  litigation but we really would have been  in a constitutional crisis  um it is to uh to to Mr Pence's credit  that he refused to go along with that  and recognize that uh in our in our  democracy the will of the voters really  is sacrosanct yet Thom Hartmann radio  host Tom Hartman has an interesting  Twitter thread from in the last week it  might be a few days ago were he kind of  outlines  what this could look like in 2024 with  the difference that there is a move to  accept different electors and that  although we all intuitively know that's  not right it's not what's supposed to  happen it would be a violation of the  will of the people all of the things  that you've said it's not so cut and dry  that it obviously fails that it could  get pretty complicated and dicey for a  period of time  it absolutely could and one of the ways  that that could happen is if state  courts that um support the losing  candidate wanted to  um sort of Muddy the waters in in  Wisconsin for example the we had a  partial recount or president Trump's  campaign asked for a recount in in the  Madison area in Milwaukee and then when  they didn't like the results of that  recount because it actually showed that  that Biden won by more votes  um they they they filed a lawsuit as  they're entitled to do to challenge the  results of the recount and that case  went up to the Wisconsin Supreme Court  the Wisconsin Supreme Court took  unprecedented actions I don't think this  had ever happened before the case came  in on a Friday afternoon the Electoral  College was meeting on Monday at noon  and that's a statutory deadline  and so the court had people brief late  at night on Friday night they held oral  argument by zoom on Saturday and they  issued a full opinion  um with all of its reasoning and  everything on Monday morning so that  they would have given the final word on  the election results in Wisconsin before  the Electoral College met but imagine I  mean Mr Eastman's arguments would be  much stronger if the court had not done  that if there was still a question about  who the legal winner in a state was  right then there is a much better  argument for these dueling slates and  you really have questions then about how  Congress is supposed to resolve this or  what they're supposed to do so we could  with what we've learned from 2020 we  could imagine in 2024 a number of actors  uh taking making specific decisions to  try to uh leave more flexibility for  Congress or the vice president or make  this uglier and harder in ways that are  really really  um dangerous to our democracy very very  scary but uh one piece of what what is  being done uh is this lawsuit and we've  been speaking with Jeffrey Mandel  president and Lead counsel at law  forward thanks so much for talking to me  today and explaining what you're what  you're doing  thanks David for having me it's a  pleasure I appreciate your attention to  this and I hope we can come back and  update you as it moves forward

